# Three trees that agree d and e are sisters but each put a somewhere else.
#
# Their clusters fit a level-2 network with two reticulations -- but that
# network does not display the three trees, only their clusters. Requiring the
# trees themselves costs a third reticulation:
#
#   phylocass examples/three_trees.newick                   level 2, 2 reticulations
#   phylocass examples/three_trees.newick --display-trees   level 3, 3 reticulations
(((a,b),c),(d,e));
(((a,c),b),(d,e));
(((a,d),b),(c,e));
